Root cause:
The bug occurs because the test `TestUserGroupInformation#testGetServerSideGroups` fails on Windows due to the inability to find the `winutils.exe` executable. This is caused by the hardcoded setting of the `hadoop.home.dir` system property to "/tmp", which does not point to the correct location of `winutils.exe` on Windows systems. The modification aims to use the `HADOOP_HOME` environment variable instead, allowing the test to locate `winutils.exe` properly.



Now, determine whether the provided code snippet is buggy:
    // doesn't matter what it is, but getGroups needs it set...
    System.setProperty("hadoop.home.dir", "/tmp");
    // fake the realm is kerberos is enabled
    System.setProperty("java.security.krb5.kdc", "");
    System.setProperty("java.security.krb5.realm", "DEFAULT.REALM");
  }


